NNAAMMEE
     yyppllddaapp..ccoonnff — LDAP YP map daemon configuration file

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ypldap(8) daemon provides YP maps using LDAP as a backend.

SSEECCTTIIOONNSS
     The yyppllddaapp..ccoonnff config file is divided into three main sections.

     MMaaccrrooss
           User-defined variables may be defined and used later, simplifying
           the configuration file.

     GGlloobbaall CCoonnffiigguurraattiioonn
           Global settings for ypldap(8).

     DDiirreeccttoorriieess
           LDAP Directory specific parameters.

MMAACCRROOSS
     Much like cpp(1) or m4(1), macros can be defined that will later be ex‐
     panded in context.  Macro names must start with a letter, digit, or un‐
     derscore, and may contain any of those characters.  Macro names may not
     be reserved words (for example, ddoommaaiinn).  Macros are not expanded inside
     quotes.

     For example:


           fixed_gecos="Pulled from LDAP"

           fixed attribute gecos $fixed_gecos

GGLLOOBBAALL CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONN
     Global settings concern the main behaviour of the daemon.

     domain _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Specify the name of the NIS domain yyppllddaapp..ccoonnff will provide.
     interval _s_e_c_o_n_d_s
             Specify the interval in seconds at which the whole directory will
             be pulled from LDAP.
     provide map _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Specify a map that should be provided by yyppllddaapp..ccoonnff The cur‐
             rently implemented maps are: passwd.byname, passwd.byuid,
             group.byname, group.bygid.

DDIIRREECCTTOORRIIEESS
     Directories are used to describe the LDAP schema and help yyppllddaapp..ccoonnff
     convert LDAP entries to passwd(5), master.passwd(5), and group(5) lines.
     A directory declaration is of the following form:

           directory "some.host" {
                   # directives
           }

     Valid directives for directories are:

     aattttrriibbuuttee _n_a_m_e mmaappss ttoo _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Map the passwd(5), master.passwd(5), or group(5) attribute to the
             LDAP attribute name supplied.

     bbaasseeddnn _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied search base as starting point for the directory
             search.

     ggrroouuppddnn _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied search base as starting point for the directory
             search for groups.  If not supplied, the basedn value will be
             used.

     bbiinnddccrreedd _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied credentials for simple authentication against
             the directory.

     bbiinnddddnn _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied Distinguished Name to bind to the directory.

     ffiixxeedd aattttrriibbuuttee _a_t_t_r_i_b_u_t_e _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Do not retrieve the specified attribute from LDAP but instead set
             it unconditionally to the supplied value for every entry.

     ggrroouupp ffiilltteerr _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied LDAP filter to retrieve group entries.

     lliisstt _n_a_m_e mmaappss ttoo _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Map the passwd(5), master.passwd(5), or group(5) attribute to the
             LDAP attribute name supplied.  A list creates a comma separated
             list of all the LDAP attributes found.

             Valid attributes are:

                   nnaammee
                   ppaasssswwdd
                   uuiidd
                   ggiidd
                   ggeeccooss
                   hhoommee
                   sshheellll
                   cchhaannggee
                   eexxppiirree
                   ccllaassss
                   ggrroouuppnnaammee
                   ggrroouuppppaasssswwdd
                   ggrroouuppggiidd
                   ggrroouuppmmeemmbbeerrss

     ppaasssswwdd ffiilltteerr _s_t_r_i_n_g
             Use the supplied LDAP filter to retrieve password entries.

